Implement two stacks based on one array.
Support these operations:

push1() // to push in the first stack
push2() // to push in the second stack
pop1()
pop2()
isEmpty1()
isEmpty2()
isFull1()
isFull2()

Make sure your implementation is space efficient.
hint: do not allocate the same amount of space by dividing the array in half.

solution: one stack start from beginning of array
          the other stack start from end of array
          when see each other
          stackoverflow!


Note: we implement two separate stack based on one aray
      so we can use it for algorithm that need two stack
      like MinStack

Note: java array does not support negative index!
      just python support this!